  "rationale": "S4 sim-playability (2026-10-08): deliberate behaviour changes and two content tunes. (1) laborObligation: the occupation demand now restates the subsistence (food) and upkeep (vellum) bills at the land's own yield share before dividing by a laborer's all-kinds output; before, it asked for under half the laborers the food bill needs and the reference universe starved at a 47% shortfall from about world year 150 (measured on origin/main 95738881, seed 20260813). Fed universes grow larger and their mages reach further. (2) The stasis stagnation clock runs only while worship tier is below the universe's recorded peak, so completion of a small square is no longer read as decline. (3) rl-open-the-portal researchCost 18343 -> 9520, the tier-4 floor. (4) change-tradition favorCost 65536 -> 61440, the tier-4 cap, since tier 5 was never reached. (5) readEdicts returns ascending handle order, the order action 7's resolver indexes, so a strategy that revokes by the index it observed revokes that edict. The provenance-only re-seal was tried first and refused: referencePeakPopulation@permissive-breadth moved +8.0 SE (300 -> 307) past a tolerance of 2.625. This is the new behaviour, not a regression.",
